        <item>
            <title>3.29.0</title>
            <pubDate>Fri, 20 Nov 2026 17:02:47 +0900</pubDate>
            <link>https://github.com/Saqoosha/Canopy</link>
            <sparkle:version>234</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>3.29.0</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>15.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <sparkle:hardwareRequirements>arm64</sparkle:hardwareRequirements>
            <description sparkle:format="markdown"><![CDATA[### Features
- The launcher's session menu now lists the selected folder's past sessions on this Mac, as it already did for another Mac's folder. Picking one resumes it; Cmd opens it in a new pane.
- Dragging a session pane's header moves the window.

### Changes
- Double-clicking the title-bar band of a pane follows the System Settings double-click action (zoom or minimize). Renaming a session is a double-click on the header's lower half.
- The launcher's session menu no longer repeats the folder name above its session list.

### Bug Fixes
- Double-clicking the window's top edge no longer opens the rename sheet.
- The settings link in Claude Code's held-message notice opens your settings.json in your default editor, instead of an empty "untitled" viewer. A second login opens its own settings file.
]]></description>
